{"name":"Vulcan","hex":"#36383c","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Vulcan","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The god of volcanoes and fire, especially the forge, also the patron of all craftsmen, especially blacksmiths. The Roman counterpart of Hephaestus.","A placename.\nA town in Vulcan County, southern Alberta, Canada.\nA volcano in Papua New Guinea.\nA place in Romania.\nA commune of Brașov County, Romania.\nA city in Hunedoara County, Romania.\nA village in the commune of Apold, Mureș County, Romania.\nA village in the commune of Ciuruleasa, Alba County, Romania.\nA place in the United States.\nA ghost town in Gunnison County, Colorado.\nAn unincorporated community in Norway Township, Dickinson County, Michigan.\nAn unincorporated community in Iron County, Missouri.\nAn inactive volcano in New Mexico, United States.\n  A hypothetical planet proposed in the 19th century to exist in an orbit between Mercury and the Sun.\n\nEllipsis of Vulcan County."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A blacksmith; a metalworker.","One who is lame (unable to walk properly), especially with a twisted or otherwise misshapen leg."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Vulcan"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vulcan (mythology)","blocks":[{"text":"Vulcan is the god of fire including the fire of volcanoes, deserts, metalworking and the forge in ancient Roman religion and myth. He is often depicted with a blacksmith's hammer. The Vulcanalia was the annual festival held August 23 in his honor. His Greek counterpart is Hephaestus, the god of fire and smithery. In Etruscan religion, he is identified with Sethlans."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Casa_di_sirico%2C_triclinium%2C_09_teti_e_vulcano.jpg/330px-Casa_di_sirico%2C_triclinium%2C_09_teti_e_vulcano.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vulcan_(mythology)","wikidata":"Q4640"},{"title":"Vulcan (Star Trek)","blocks":[{"text":"Vulcans are a fictional extraterrestrial humanoid species in the Star Trek media franchise. They are noted for their strict adherence to logic and reason and suppression of emotion. Known for their pronounced eyebrows and pointed ears, they originate from the fictional planet Vulcan."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Spock_and_T%27Pring.jpg/330px-Spock_and_T%27Pring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vulcan_(Star_Trek)","wikidata":"Q6497384"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Bas_relief_from_Arch_of_Marcus_Aurelius_showing_sacrifice.jpg/500px-Bas_relief_from_Arch_of_Marcus_Aurelius_showing_sacrifice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Bas_relief_from_Arch_of_Marcus_Aurelius_showing_sacrifice.jpg/1280px-Bas_relief_from_Arch_of_Marcus_Aurelius_showing_sacrifice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Bas_relief_from_Arch_of_Marcus_Aurelius_showing_sacrifice.jpg/500px-Bas_relief_from_Arch_of_Marcus_Aurelius_showing_sacrifice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABas_relief_from_Arch_of_Marcus_Aurelius_showing_sacrifice.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Andrea_Mantegna_045.jpg/500px-Andrea_Mantegna_045.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Andrea_Mantegna_045.jpg/1280px-Andrea_Mantegna_045.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Andrea_Mantegna_045.jpg/500px-A